// M006 -- SMG arm. defender = monitor/check placement, attacker = CAN spoof
// timing under budget b. Stackelberg by construction: the defender's memory
// budget m is fixed in the model, the attacker chooses when to spend.

// P1: the defender's game value -- the collision probability it can guarantee
// against a worst-case attacker.
<<defender>>Pmin=? [ F "unsafe" ]

// P2: the same value read from the attacker's side. Determinacy says these are
// equal; computed independently, this is the primary invariant gate.
<<attacker>>Pmax=? [ F "unsafe" ]

// P3: the safety-objective dual. <<defender>>Pmax[G !unsafe] must equal
// 1 - <<defender>>Pmin[F unsafe]. Second, independent gate.
<<defender>>Pmax=? [ G !"unsafe" ]

// P4: expected time to detection under an adversarial attacker. Infinity means
// the attacker can avoid ever tripping the monitor.
<<defender>>R{"time"}min=? [ F "latched" ]

// P5: can the defender force detection at all?
<<defender>>Pmax=? [ F "latched" ]
